# Docker Build Strategy: Whitelist specific source files to minimize context size.
# JARs and large tools are downloaded at build time, not shipped in context.

# 1. Ignore EVERYTHING
**

# 2. Whitelist Source Code & Config
!**/*.py
!**/*.sh
!**/*.brf
!**/*.xml
!**/*.txt
!**/*.md
!**/*.properties
!**/*.bat
!batch_docker.xml
!clean.sh

# 3. Explicitly Re-ignore Large/Binary Assets
**/*.zip
**/*.obf
**/*.pbf
**/*.o5m
**/*.gpkg
**/*.osm
**/*.json
**/*.log
**/*.jar
**/nodes.tmp.odb
**/regions.ocbf
**/temp_map_build/
**/segments4/
**/dist/
**/srtm/
**/osmand_input/
**/osmand_output/
**/osmand_gen/

# 4. Ignore Git and IDE metadata
.git/
.idea/
.vscode/
__pycache__/
